he's sucked up to Europe, he's sucked up to the trade unions, he's spent too much money, he hasn't been a real conservative. And you can get away with this sort of thing if you win. But Heath has lost two elections in nine months. Because presumably that brands his kind of conservatism as a conservatism for losers. People don't want it. Yeah, completely. If you're not red-blooded and then you don't win, what's the point?
