So there's this, there's this sort of instinctive, emotional thirst for more robust, more obviously conservative politics. But there's also an intellectual, more ideological side to it. So since 1955, a think tank called the Institute for Economic Affairs has been arguing that Britain has gone much too far down the road to socialism. And it's been calling, like a voice in the wilderness for privatisation of nationalised industries, for colourisation. the welfare state for bringing back free market economics, kind of laissez-faire economics that you would have found in the 19th century under the sort of Gladstone administration and whatnot. And part of this is the adoption of a new creed, which in some ways is quite an old creed, which is monetarism.
所以有一种本能的、情感上的渴望，想要更强硬、更明显的保守派政治。但它也有一个知识性的、更意识形态的一面。所以自1955年以来，一个名为“经济事务研究所”的智库一直在争论，英国在社会主义道路上走得太远了。它一直在呼吁——就像旷野中的声音——私有化国有工业，福利国家，恢复自由市场经济，那种你在19世纪格莱斯顿政府下会发现的自由放任经济等等。而这其中的一部分是采用了一种新的信条，在某些方面也是一种相当古老的信条，即货币主义。

